title: Myeloproliferative neoplasms
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The classical BCR::ABL1-negative myeloproliferative neoplasms share activated JAK–STAT signaling, but treatment priorities differ.

* [[Essential thrombocythemia]]: prevent thrombosis while recognizing acquired von Willebrand syndrome and bleeding.
* [[Polycythemia vera]]: prevent thrombosis; maintain hematocrit <45% and select cytoreduction by vascular risk and disease burden.
* [[Primary myelofibrosis]]: estimate survival and transplant candidacy separately from symptoms; see [[Management of myelofibrosis]].

Sources: ASH-SAP, 9th ed. (2025), ch. 37, p. 448; ASCO-SEP 2026, ch. 19, pp. 1070–1076; NCCN Myeloproliferative Neoplasms v2.2026 (June 16, 2026), MPN-2; Discussion MS-9–10, MS-39–40.
